# Backend (Spring Boot)

## Layering
- Controllers stay thin; business logic in `application/service`
- Do not inject repositories into controllers except trivial admin read-only cases already present
- Prefer typed API errors over bare `RuntimeException` for new code

## Multi-shop
- Catalog, stock, settings, vouchers, orders, users, branches, licenses are shop-scoped
- Resolve shop from the authenticated user; never trust client `shopId` alone for writes
- Default seeded shop must keep single-shop installs working

## Caching
- Use Spring Cache + Caffeine for menu/settings/active vouchers
- Evict on every related create/update/delete
- Do not add Redis unless multi-instance deploy is required

## Storage
- Upload via `StorageService` only — never write into `frontend/src/assets`
- Keep S3 implementation ready; local disk is default for single-machine POS

## Security
- No default secrets in committed prod config; env vars for JWT/DB/API keys
- Do not expose password-hash utilities publicly
- Staff APIs require authentication
